$DIR/main.p:29:6: r holds a view of b (first(&b), line 27), which was moved into take2 (its parameter takes a Buf by value) at line 28, so r can no longer be used here
    r looks at memory that b owns, without owning it: the view was made by
    first(&b) at line 27. A view of an owner held in a local variable may be
    used only while the variable keeps the value the view was made from. At line
    28 b was moved into take2 (its parameter takes a Buf by value), so the view
    may look at memory that was released, or at a value that now belongs to
    something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use r before line 28, or move b only after the last use of r
    Or move a copy at line 28, so that b keeps its value:
        b.Clone()
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)
